posts.text:
Did the jury just hear the most important evidence in the Lindsay Clancy trial... only to be told to disregard it?

With the defense arguing psychosis and the prosecution arguing premeditation, the case may hinge on a single question: Did she understand the gravity of what she was doing?

@allenmendenhall is a Research Fellow in Economic Policy Studies and Senior Advisor for the Free Enterprise Initiative at The Heritage Foundation.

